# Refresh / input / animation period, in ms.  Kconfig help: "Default display
# refresh, input device read and animation step period."  One knob, three
# effects -- and it is the cause of the "sluggish scrolling" complaint.
#
# Why 33 is too slow (the old default):
#   - display refresh  -> animations capped at 30 FPS
#   - INPUT DEVICE READ -> lv_indev.c:128 creates the touch read timer with
#     this same period, so the panel was sampled at only 30 Hz.  A drag only
#     produced a new coordinate every 33 ms, which is what makes scrolling
#     feel steppy and imprecise.
#   - animation step   -> 30 steps/s
#
# Why 16 is affordable: measured on hardware 2026-10-16 with LVGL's own
# sysmon, a redraw costs render 6-8 ms + flush 2-3 ms (~10 ms), with CPU at
# 0-5% (peak 53%) while idle.  A 16 ms frame budget (62 FPS) therefore has
# headroom, and LVGL only repaints when something is actually invalidated --
# so a shorter period costs nothing while the UI is idle; it only buys
# smoothness while animating or scrolling.
#
# The touch panel can feed it: FT6146 is interrupt driven here
# (CONFIG_INPUT_FT6146_POLL_MS=0), reporting as soon as the controller has a
# sample, at a native rate well above 30 Hz.  We were the bottleneck, not it.
CONFIG_LV_DEF_REFR_PERIOD=16

