#
# Audio capture gain. Kconfig default is 6, but that compensates for boards
# whose multi-channel DMIC downmix dilutes the signal when only one mic is
# populated (see packages/ai_agent/Kconfig:215 help text).
#
# This board is a SINGLE analog MEMS mic wired straight to AUDCODEC ADC CH0
# in mono (sf32lb52_audcodec.c: "MEMS MIC -> audcodec ADC CH0", 16k/16bit/mono).
# There is no downmix loss to compensate, so the x6 was pure digital gain that
# only CLIPPED the signal: on hardware (2026-10-16) 2.37% of speech samples
# were clamped to +/-32767, while dividing by 6 showed the ADC peak at just
# 16.7% of full scale - the ADC was never overdriven. Digital gain adds no SNR,
# only distortion.
#
# 1 = no digital gain, full dynamic range preserved.
# NOTE: keep this file ASCII-only; non-ASCII comments break CMake configure
#       (nuttx_kconfig.cmake:48 string REGEX needs at least 5 arguments).
CONFIG_AI_AGENT_AUDIO_CAPTURE_GAIN=1
